  "id": "roads",
  "name": "Paying for roads: the marijuana tax, the gas tax swap and tax changes",
  "blurb": "Fixing Michigan's roads has been a campaign promise for years. The October 2025 budget deal paired new road money with tax changes: a new 24% wholesale tax on marijuana, a switch from the sales tax on gas to a higher fuel tax dedicated to roads, and an income tax bill that adds state deductions for tips and overtime, keeps Michigan from adopting some federal business tax breaks, and shifts corporate income tax money to roads. Supporters call it a long-term road fix with tax relief for workers; opponents objected to the new marijuana tax and to higher state business taxes.",
