    "tie": "Changes the paid sick time law that took effect the same day.",
    "what": "Rewrites the Earned Sick Time Act: one hour of paid sick time for every 30 hours worked; up to 72 hours a year at most employers and 40 hours at businesses with 10 or fewer workers, which were not covered until Oct 1, 2025; and new rules on notice and documentation (House Fiscal Agency analysis as enrolled, revised 2-27-25). Sponsor: Rep. Jay DeBoyer. House passage 67-38, 5 not voting (Jan 23, 2025); Senate passage of a substitute 26-10, 1 excused (Feb 20, 2025); House concurrence 81-29 (Feb 20, 2025). Approved by the Governor Feb 21, 2025.",
